{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"triumphant-dated-kingsnake","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## What happens\n\n`scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py <change> --revision <abbreviated-sha>` compares the\ncaller's `--revision` string against the change's full `current_revision` and, because\nan abbreviation never equals a full SHA, refuses with a staleness error naming two\nSHAs that are visibly the same commit:\n\n```\n$ python scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py 3149 --revision bed4448e175\nrefusing stale submit: inspected bed4448e175, current is bed4448e175bb0b7c28fce7d22ab673d65cfadec\n```\n\nObserved 2026-10-30 submitting Gerrit 3149. Re-running with the full 40-character SHA\nsubmitted successfully, so the change was never stale.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe message asserts a condition that is false. It names the guard's real purpose —\n\"another session uploaded a newer revision\" — in a case where no such upload happened,\nso the obvious reading is that a concurrent session raced you. The correct response\n(re-run with a longer SHA) is not discoverable from the output, and the incorrect\nresponse (re-poll, re-push, or investigate a phantom race) costs a vote cycle.\n\nAbbreviated SHAs are the natural input here: `git rev-parse --short HEAD`, `git log\n--oneline`, and the `%h` format all produce them, and every other `git` command in the\nlanding workflow accepts them.\n\n## Two defects, one fix site\n\n1. The comparison is string equality where it should be commit identity. An\n   abbreviation that uniquely prefixes the current revision denotes that revision.\n2. The error conflates \"the revision you named is not the current one\" with \"the\n   revision you named is not in the form I compare against\".\n\n## Change\n\nIn the revision guard, treat the supplied `--revision` as a match when it is a\ncase-insensitive prefix of the change's `current_revision` and is long enough to be\nunambiguous (Gerrit's own minimum is 7). Keep rejecting a value that is not a prefix —\nthat is the real stale case the guard exists for, and it must stay.\n\nWhen the value is neither a prefix nor a plausible SHA at all, say so distinctly rather\nthan reusing the staleness wording.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] **AC1** `python scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py <n> --revision <first 11 chars of\n      current_revision>` on a change whose votes are green submits it, exiting 0, and\n      does not print \"refusing stale submit\".\n- [ ] **AC2** The same invocation with the full 40-character SHA still submits, exiting 0.\n- [ ] **AC3** An invocation naming a *different* commit's full SHA still refuses and\n      exits non-zero, with the staleness wording intact.\n- [ ] **AC4** An invocation with a prefix shorter than 7 characters is refused with a\n      message that names the length requirement and does not use the staleness wording.\n- [ ] **AC5** A unit test covers all 4 cases above against a stubbed Gerrit detail\n      response, with no network access.\n- [ ] **AC6** `make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nSurfacing the HTTP 409 response body on a genuine stale submit. That is a separate\nreporting gap in the same script and is tracked on its own ticket; this change must not\nalter the 409 path.","id":"1416-a422-a3d8-4611","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"gerrit_safe_submit.py rejects an abbreviated revision SHA as \"stale\""},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793376492350379294,"uuid":"e4d11332-a51e-4432-b24d-a6a5442e2c05"}